<AddOnInstructionDefinitions Use="Context">
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Use="Target" Name="P_PTComp" Revision="3.1" RevisionExtension="01 Release" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="false" CreatedDate="2009-09-17T21:01:12.921Z" CreatedBy="Not Available" EditedDate="2014-09-03T14:38:31.870Z"
 EditedBy="PROCESS\Library" SoftwareRevision="v18.02">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Press / Temp Compensator]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details. Unmodified, up-rev only for V3.1-01 public release.]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.

This Instruction takes its primary input (analog) from a flowmeter or
differential pressure transmitter, plus inputs for actual temperature
and pressure, and uses them to calculate a compensated flow,
in other words, flow at standard temperature and pressure.
(With appropriate factors, this is a Mass Flow Rate.)

The calculation is based on the ideal gas law (PV=nRT),
so as the fluid in question deviates from an ideal gas,
this method becomes less accurate.

This instruction should NOT be used for steam or natural gas;
industry standard calculations based on the detailed properties of those
fluids (steam tables, AGA/API standards, etc.) should be used instead.

If the absolute value of the calculated flow rate is less than a
configured low flow cutoff, the flow is reported as zero.
(This helps keep flow totalizers from accumulating
an offset zero value when flow is stopped.)]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
<Parameter Name="EnableIn" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Input - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="EnableOut" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Enable Output - System Defined Parameter]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Inp_T_Act" TagType="Base" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="false" Visible="true" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Actual (Measured) Temperature, can be abs. or common units
(e.g., F or C)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Inp_P_Act" TagType="Base" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="false" Visible="true" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Actual (Measured) Pressure, can be abs. or  common units (e.g., PSIG)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Inp_DP_Act" TagType="Base" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="false" Visible="true" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Actual (Measured) Differential Pressure (e.g., "WC)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Inp_F_Act" TagType="Base" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="false" Visible="true" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Actual (Measured) Uncompensated Flow in volumetric units (e.g., CFM)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Cfg_LoFlowCutoff" TagType="Base" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[If Out_Flow is less than this cutoff value, it is shown as 0.0]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Cfg_T_Std" TagType="Base" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Standard Temperature in Inp_T_Act units
(e.g., F or C)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Cfg_P_Std" TagType="Base" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Standard Pressure in Inp_P_Act units (e.g., PSIG)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Cfg_T_Offset" TagType="Base" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA['Zero' input-units Temperature in absolute units (e.g., R or K)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>33 93 88 43</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="273.15"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Cfg_P_Offset" TagType="Base" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA['Zero' input-units Pressure in Absolute units (e.g., PSIA)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>D1 22 6B 41</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="14.696"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Cfg_DP_Ref" TagType="Base" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Reference (full- scale) Differential Pressure (e.g., "WC)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 C8 42</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="100.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Cfg_F_Ref" TagType="Base" DataType="REAL" Usage="Input" Radix="Float" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Reference Flow in volumetric units (e.g., CFM) at Reference DP]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 80 3F</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="1.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Cfg_UseDP" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Input" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1=Use Inp_DP_Act (sq.rt. curve) to calculate flow, 0=Use Inp_F_Act (linear)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Out_Flow" TagType="Base" DataType="REAL" Usage="Output" Radix="Float" Required="false" Visible="true" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Compensated Flow (at Standard Temperature and Pressure: Mass Flow)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Sts_Err" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1=Invalid Configuration, see Err_ bits]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Err_T_Std" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1=Invalid Standard Temperature (T_Std + T_Offset must be > 0.0)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Err_P_Std" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1=Invalid Standard Pressure (P_Std + P_Offset must be > 0.0)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Err_DP_Ref" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1=Invalid Reference Differential Pressure (must be > 0.0 if DP used)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Err_F_Ref" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[1=Invalid Reference Flow (at Reference DP) (must be > 0.0 if DP used)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="P_PTComp" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Unique Parameter Name for auto - discovery]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
</Parameters>
<LocalTags>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Factor" DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Calculated Flow Factor (sq.rt. of this times Ref Flow = Comp Flow)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Flow" DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Calculated Flow (subject to negation)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="REAL" Radix="Float" Value="0.0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Inf_Type" DataType="STRING_16" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Must contain AOI name, used for HMI and Information S/W]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>08 00 00 00 50 5F 50 54 43 6F 6D 70 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="8">
<![CDATA['P_PTComp']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Inf_Tab" DataType="SINT" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Tab to display (FTView ME)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="SINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Cfg_Tag" DataType="STRING_20" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Tagname for display on HMI]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>08 00 00 00 50 5F 50 54 43 6F 6D 70 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="8">
<![CDATA['P_PTComp']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Cfg_Label" DataType="STRING_20" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Label for graphic symbol displayed on HMI]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>12 00 00 00 46 6C 6F 77 20 61 74 20 53 74 64 2E 
20 43 6F 6E 64 2E 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="18">
<![CDATA['Flow at Std. Cond.']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Cfg_Desc" DataType="STRING_40" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Description for display on HMI]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>27 00 00 00 50 72 65 73 73 75 72 65 20 2F 20 54 
65 6D 70 65 72 61 74 75 72 65 20 43 6F 6D 70 65 
6E 73 61 74 65 64 20 46 6C 6F 77 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="39">
<![CDATA['Pressure / Temperature Compensated Flow']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Inf_Lib" DataType="STRING_12" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Display Library for Faceplate call-up]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>06 00 00 00 52 41 2D 42 41 53 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="6">
<![CDATA['RA-BAS']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Calculated Flow at Standard Temperature and Pressure]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
P_PTComp :  PROCESS -- PRESSURE / TEMPERATURE COMPENSATOR
============================================================
Revision 3.1-01 Release  2014-09-03:  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V2.x Revision History archived.
V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib.
V3.0-01  2014-01-22:  Modified compensation calculations.
V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Unmodified for Library of Process Objects V3.1, up-rev only.
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Unmodified, up-rev only for V3.1-01 public release.
============================================================
This Instruction takes its primary input (analog) from a flowmeter or
differential pressure transmitter, plus inputs for actual temperature
and pressure, and uses them to calculate a compensated flow,
in other words, flow at standard temperature and pressure.
(With appropriate factors, this is a Mass Flow Rate.)

The calculation is based on the ideal gas law (PV=nRT),
so as the fluid in question deviates from an ideal gas,
this method becomes less accurate.

This instruction should NOT be used for steam or natural gas;
industry standard calculations based on the detailed properties of those
fluids (steam tables, AGA/API standards, etc.) should be used instead.

If the absolute value of the calculated flow rate is less than a
configured low flow cutoff, the flow is reported as zero.
(This helps keep flow totalizers from accumulating
an offset zero value when flow is stopped.)
============================================================
SHOW LOCAL STRINGS
============================================================
The STRINGs containing the text associated with each instance of this
instruction cannot be Input or Output Parameters, because STRINGs are not
 'atomic' types. (Inputs and Outputs must be SINT, INT, DINT, REAL, or BOOL.)

In order to make it easier to find and configure these STRINGs, this rung
was added.  THE JMP (and the LBL on the following rung)
MUST NOT BE REMOVED!!!

To view the STRINGs, go to the instruction instance (in LD or FBD), RIGHT-click
to bring up the context menu and select "Open Instruction Logic".
This rung will appear with the STRING values for the selected instance.
You may double-click the STRING values here to modify them as well.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(SkipText)CONCAT(Cfg_Desc,Cfg_Label,Cfg_Tag)LOWER(Inf_Lib,Inf_Type);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CONFIGURATION PROCESSING
============================================================
These rungs handle Configuration Data:

Check Cfg_T_Std (Standard Temperature).

The Standard Temperature IN ABSOLUTE TEMPERATURE UNITS
 must be greater than 0.0.

HOWEVER: Cfg_T_Std is in "familiar" temperature units -- Celsius or Fahrenheit.
So (Cfg_T_Std + Cfg_T_Offset) must be > 0.0 and < +Inf.

Cfg_T_Std is the Standard (Reference) Temperature in the same units as Inp_T_Act.
Cfg_T_Offset is the absolute temperature when Inp_T_Act is zero.

Typical values for Cfg_T_Offset are 273.15 --- Kelvins, for Inp_T_Act in Celsius,
or 459.67 --- Rankine, for Inp_T_Act in Fahrenheit.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SkipText)[CMP(((Cfg_T_Std + Cfg_T_Offset) <= 0.0)) ,CMP(((Cfg_T_Std + Cfg_T_Offset) > 3.402823e38)) ]OTE(Err_T_Std);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Check Cfg_P_Std (Standard Pressure).
The Standard Pressure IN ABSOLUTE PRESSURE UNITS
 must be greater than 0.0.

HOWEVER:  Cfg_P_Std is assumed to be a gauge pressure.
So (Cfg_P_Std + Cfg_P_Offset) must be > 0.0 and < +Inf.

Cfg_P_Std is the Standard (Reference) Pressure in the same units as Inp_P_Act (gauge pressure).
Cfg_P_Offset is the absolute pressure when Inp_P_Act is zero.

A typical value for Cfg_P_Offset is 14.696 --- in PSIA]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CMP((Cfg_P_Std + Cfg_P_Offset) <= 0.0) ,CMP((Cfg_P_Std + Cfg_P_Offset) > 3.402823e38) ]OTE(Err_P_Std);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Differential Pressure Input is used, check Cfg_DP_Ref (Reference
Differential Pressure) and Cfg_F_Ref (Reference Flow at Reference DP).

The Reference Differential Pressure IN PRESSURE DIFFERENCE UNITS
 must be greater than 0.0 and less than +Inf..
The Reference Flow (at Reference DP) in FLOW (at S.T.P.) UNITS
must be greater than 0.0 and less than +Inf..]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_UseDP)[[LEQ(Cfg_DP_Ref,0.0) ,GRT(Cfg_DP_Ref,3.402823e38) ] OTE(Err_DP_Ref) ,[LEQ(Cfg_F_Ref,0.0) ,GRT(Cfg_F_Ref,3.402823e38) ] OTE(Err_F_Ref) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If any of the Configuration values is invalid, skip further processing
and exit with an Error Status.  (Set the calculated flow to zero.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Err_T_Std) ,XIC(Err_P_Std) ,XIC(Err_DP_Ref) ,XIC(Err_F_Ref) ]OTE(Sts_Err)CLR(Wrk_Flow)JMP(End);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The selected Input must be a valid REAL number.
If it is Infinite (-1.$, 1.$),Indeterminate (-1.#IND) or Not a Number (-1.#QNAN or 1.#QNAN),
skip the calculations and return the input REAL exception value instead.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Cfg_UseDP) [LEQ(Inp_DP_Act,-3.402823e38) ,GRT(Inp_DP_Act,3.402823e38) ] COP(Inp_DP_Act,Wrk_Flow,1) ,XIO(Cfg_UseDP) [LEQ(Inp_F_Act,-3.402823e38) ,GRT(Inp_F_Act,3.402823e38) ] COP(Inp_F_Act,Wrk_Flow,1) ]JMP(End);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CALCULATE COMPENSATED FLOW
============================================================
This first CPT calculates   T_std_abs / T_act_abs * P_act_abs / P_std_abs.
This factor is common to both means of calculating flow, below.

Absolute temperatures and pressures are calculated by adding the configured
offsets (Cfg_T_Offset, Cfg_P_Offset) to each Standard or Actual T or P value.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(Wrk_Factor,((Cfg_T_Std+Cfg_T_Offset)/(Inp_T_Act+Cfg_T_Offset)*(Inp_P_Act+Cfg_P_Offset)/(Cfg_P_Std+Cfg_P_Offset)));]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the flow calculation uses the Differential Pressure (DP) Input
(Cfg_UseDP = 1), this rung calculates the flow as follows:

Flow =  Flow_ref * ( T_std_abs / T_act_abs ) * ( P_act_abs / P_std_abs ) * SQRT ( DP_act / DP_ref )

and if the DP is negative, reports a negative (reverse) flow.

#####  V3.0-01  2014-01-20:  Modified compensation calculation.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_UseDP)[CPT(Wrk_Flow,Cfg_F_Ref*Wrk_Factor*SQR(ABS(Inp_DP_Act)/Cfg_DP_Ref)) ,LES(Inp_DP_Act,0.0) NEG(Wrk_Flow,Wrk_Flow) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the flow calculation uses the Uncompensated Flow Input
(Cfg_UseDP = 0, default), this rung calculates the Compensated Flow as follows:

Flow_comp =  Flow_uncomp * ( T_std_abs / T_act_abs ) * ( P_act_abs / P_std_abs )

The sign of the Output (compensated) Flow follows the sign of the Input (uncompensated) flow.
(All the values in the "factor" form above should be positive, so "factor" is positive.)

#####  V3.0-01  2014-01-20:  Simplified calculation.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Cfg_UseDP)MUL(Inp_F_Act,Wrk_Factor,Wrk_Flow);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Finally, if the ABSOLUTE VALUE of the calculated flow is LESS THAN
the configured LOW CUTOFF value (default = 0.0), report ZERO flow.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CMP(ABS(Wrk_Flow)<Cfg_LoFlowCutoff)CLR(Wrk_Flow);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Whatever flow we determined (and it might be Inf, NaN, if the input is Inf, NaN),
copy it to the output.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(End)COP(Wrk_Flow,Out_Flow,1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
<Dependencies>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_40"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_20"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_12"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_16"/>
</Dependencies>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
